=== A. x11 without termux-x11 installed
spft: termux-x11 is not installed. In Termux run:  pkg install x11-repo  and then  pkg install termux-x11-nightly
     (and install the Termux:X11 app: the file termux-x11-universal-debug.apk from
      https://github.com/termux/termux-x11/releases/tag/nightly - or run: bash install.sh)
exit=1

=== B. x11 called as root
spft: run spft from Termux as a normal user (it calls su itself)
exit=1

=== C. x11, first run (server not running yet)
>> starting the Termux:X11 server
>> setting up the Termux:X11 display: landscape, fullscreen, zoom 150%
   additionalKbdVisible: true -> false
   fullscreen: false -> true
   forceOrientation: portrait -> landscape
   displayScale: 100 -> 150
   displayResolutionMode: native -> scaled
   displayFilteringMode: nearest -> bilinear
exit=0
--- calls:
termux-x11 :0
am start --user 0 -n com.termux.x11/com.termux.x11.MainActivity
wake-lock
mount -o bind /dev $T/root/dev
mount -o bind /dev/pts $T/root/dev/pts
mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,size=256m tmpfs $T/root/dev/shm
mount -t proc proc $T/root/proc
mount -t sysfs sysfs $T/root/sys
mount -o bind $T/pfx/tmp/.X11-unix $T/root/tmp/.X11-unix
--- command line handed to chroot (one argument per line):
$T/root
/usr/bin/env
-i
HOME=/root
TERM=xterm
LANG=C.UTF-8
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
/bin/bash
-lc
SPFT_DISPLAY=x11 spft-run
--- helpers written inside Debian:
-rwxr-xr-x spft-gui
-rwxr-xr-x spft-run
spft-run identical to lib/run.sh
spft-gui identical to lib/gui.sh
--- file-dialog shortcuts (top level of Debian, then Debian's home):
/sdcard -> /mnt/sdcard
~/Download -> /mnt/sdcard/Download
~/sdcard -> /mnt/sdcard
--- the root step ran a copy kept under Termux's own folder:
lib spft 
copy of lib/run.sh is identical
--- Termux:X11 settings now (the app started out in portrait, at the phone's own size):
fullscreen=true forceOrientation=landscape displayScale=150 displayResolutionMode=scaled displayFilteringMode=bilinear additionalKbdVisible=false showAdditionalKbd=true touchMode=1 
--- saved for 'x11 reset':
fullscreen:false forceOrientation:portrait displayScale:100 displayResolutionMode:native displayFilteringMode:nearest additionalKbdVisible:true 
--- the phone was kept awake: wake-lock calls = 1

