=== I. stop closes the tool and lets the phone sleep again; a second stop finds nothing
stopped 1 process(es) that were running inside Debian
removed an old Termux:X11 socket (no server was running)
exit=0
ok: the tool process is gone
wake-unlock calls: 1
stopped 0 process(es) that were running inside Debian
exit=0

=== I2. stop also stops the Termux:X11 server, and removes the socket that a killed server leaves behind
-- a server is running (its process is called "termux-x11 <app id> :0")
stopped 0 process(es) that were running inside Debian
stopped the Termux:X11 server
exit=0
ok: the server process is gone
ok: the socket file is gone
-- only a socket file is left (the server was killed): it is removed, so that the next spft starts a new server
stopped 0 process(es) that were running inside Debian
removed an old Termux:X11 socket (no server was running)
exit=0
ok: the stale socket is gone
-- nothing at all: nothing to report
0

