=== O2. an app version without forceOrientation: the by-hand steps are shown
>> setting up the Termux:X11 display: landscape, fullscreen, zoom 150%
   additionalKbdVisible: true -> false
   fullscreen: false -> true
   displayScale: 100 -> 150
   displayResolutionMode: native -> scaled
   displayFilteringMode: nearest -> bilinear
   not applied: forceOrientation(not in this app version)
   By hand instead: in the Termux:X11 app open Preferences > Output and set
     Screen orientation = landscape    Fullscreen = on    Display resolution mode = scaled    Display scale, % = 150
exit=0
tool started: 1

=== P. the Termux:X11 app does not answer (about 8 s)
>> setting up the Termux:X11 display: landscape, fullscreen, zoom 150%
>> the Termux:X11 app did not answer, so its settings were not changed
   By hand instead: in the Termux:X11 app open Preferences > Output and set
     Screen orientation = landscape    Fullscreen = on    Display resolution mode = scaled    Display scale, % = 150
exit=0
settings unchanged: fullscreen=false forceOrientation=portrait displayScale=100 displayResolutionMode=native displayFilteringMode=nearest additionalKbdVisible=true showAdditionalKbd=true touchMode=1 
tool started: 1

=== Q. a Termux:X11 package without termux-x11-preference
>> termux-x11-preference is missing (try: pkg upgrade termux-x11-nightly), so the display can't be set up for you
   By hand instead: in the Termux:X11 app open Preferences > Output and set
     Screen orientation = landscape    Fullscreen = on    Display resolution mode = scaled    Display scale, % = 150
exit=0
tool started: 1

=== X. spft check (the Termux part, then the phone part) with the Termux:X11 app installed
== Termux ==
root     : su found
x11-pkg  : installed
x11-app  : Termux:X11 app installed
storage  : run termux-setup-storage once if you want Termux to see your Download folder (optional)
== phone and Debian ==
kernel   : 64-bit ARM (CONFIG_ARM64=y) - OK, a 32-bit Android userspace doesn't matter
cdc_acm  : MISSING - this kernel was built without it (CONFIG_USB_ACM), so SP Flash Tool can't see a device from this phone (use mtkclient instead)
chroot   : $T/sysbin/chroot
android  : unknown (API ?), ABIs: ?
debian   : installed in $T/root
box64    : missing - run: spft install
tool     : NOT installed - run: spft tool
exit=0

=== X1. cdc_acm: what the kernel config says when the driver folder is missing
-- FAKE_ACM=m
cdc_acm  : NOT LOADED - this kernel has the driver as a module. Try:  su -c 'modprobe cdc_acm'  and run spft check again
-- FAKE_ACM=y
cdc_acm  : not found, although the kernel config says it is built in. If the target is never detected, use another host phone (or mtkclient)
-- FAKE_ACM=n
cdc_acm  : MISSING - this kernel was built without it (CONFIG_USB_ACM), so SP Flash Tool can't see a device from this phone (use mtkclient instead)
-- FAKE_ACM=none
cdc_acm  : not found, and the kernel config can't be read to tell why. If the target is never detected, use another host phone (or mtkclient)
-- FAKE_ACM=(option not in the config)
cdc_acm  : MISSING - this kernel was built without it (CONFIG_USB_ACM), so SP Flash Tool can't see a device from this phone (use mtkclient instead)

=== X2. ... with the app missing
x11-app  : NOT installed - get termux-x11-universal-debug.apk: https://github.com/termux/termux-x11/releases/tag/nightly
exit=0

